      "id": "ZH-2-01",
      "severity": "MINOR",
      "key": "composition of ui.chat.canonical.image_gen.cancel.running + …cancel.checking (callsite, not a draft value)",
      "current": "… 若产出音频则会计费。 正在确认结算。  (the two values joined by one ASCII space)",
      "evidence": "Independently verified at src/renderer/src/features/chat/canonical/image-gen-card.tsx:341, where runningStopSentence composes `${running} ${t(...cancel.checking)}` with a hard-coded ASCII space. In zh-CN both values end in the full-width 。 so the joined line carries a half-width space between two Chinese sentences, which is visibly off in Chinese typography and repeats in every stop-with-settlement state. The two VALUES themselves are correct; nothing in the zh-CN draft needs rewording. The programme already solved this shape once: ui.chat.sidebar.mark_all_read.scope_joined is \"{chats} {tokenless}\" in en and \"{chats}{tokenless}\" in zh-CN.",
      "suggested": "Key the joiner rather than hard-coding a space (en \" \", zh-CN \"\"), mirroring scope_joined, and pass it through the same t() binding so a language switch repaints it. Not a draft change and not in this audit's edit scope; recorded because it is user-visible.",
      "gating": false
    }
  ],
